  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Friendly Neighborhood Pharmacist",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Friendly Neighborhood Pharmacist\"**\n\nKind, expert, calm. The app looks like a well-run pharmacy counter: a deep green-teal shell, a cool white-green ground, and plain white panels with hairline edges. Nothing is decorated; everything is labeled. Every answer ends in a plain instruction, and the instruction is always presented the same way, as a pharmacy-style label with a colored \"WHAT TO DO\" band over one sentence.\n\nDensity is low and type is large, because the reader is a senior who may be stressed, may have low vision, and may tap with a tremor. Sizes are in points and scale with the phone's text-size setting; nothing drops below 16. The world follows the phone into light or dark, and both schemes are first-class: every text color clears 4.5:1 on the surfaces it sits on. The visual rejections are confirmed by the direction: not the shield-and-navy security app, and not the cream-and-serif \"cozy\" app.\n\nThe platform is adaptive. Fonts are the platform's own (SF on iOS, Roboto on Android), icons are SF Symbols on iOS and Material Symbols elsewhere, and navigation is the native bottom tab bar with each platform's own selected-state idiom.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Teal shell, cool white-green ground, white hairline cards, no shadows.",
      "Senior type scale: body 20, headings 22 to 32 at heavy weights, floor 16.",
      "Touch targets at least 56 tall; every control carries a text label.",
      "Red, amber, and green speak only inside instruction strips and verdicts.",
      "One signature component: the instruction strip."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Verdict-Only Color Rule",
        "body": "Red, amber, and green appear only inside an instruction strip or as verdict text. They never tint a card, a button, an icon, or a heading on their own.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Words-First Rule",
        "body": "Color repeats what the words say, never replaces them. A strip always carries its label text; a verdict always carries its sentence.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two-Scheme Rule",
        "body": "Every new color is added to both `light` and `dark` in `Palette`, and every text pairing is checked at 4.5:1 in both.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sixteen Floor Rule",
        "body": "No text below 16. Body is 20.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Text Component Rule",
        "body": "All text goes through `AppText` with a `variant` from the scale and a `tone` from the palette; no ad-hoc font sizes in screens.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Band-Only Label Rule",
        "body": "The uppercase `label` style names an instruction strip. It is never placed above a heading as an eyebrow or kicker.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline-Not-Shadow Rule",
        "body": "A container is distinguished by a 1px `border` and a surface change, never by a shadow or elevation.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** take every color from `useColors()` or `makeStyles()`, and define new roles in both light and dark.",
      "**Do** end every answer with an instruction strip holding one plain imperative sentence.",
      "**Do** keep controls at least 56 tall (`minTouchTarget`) with a visible text label.",
      "**Do** use `AppText` variants for all text; body at 20, nothing below 16.",
      "**Do** separate containers with a 1px `border` hairline on `surface`, radius 16.",
      "**Do** keep one filled button per screen; use tonal for the rest."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add shadows or elevation to cards, bars, or buttons.",
      "**Don't** use red, amber, or green outside instruction strips and verdict text.",
      "**Don't** put an uppercase label above a heading as an eyebrow or kicker; the `label` style belongs to the strip band.",
      "**Don't** add colored side borders to cards or strips.",
      "**Don't** ship an icon-only control.",
      "**Don't** nest cards.",
      "**Don't** use `border` (the decorative hairline) as the only edge of an input; inputs take `border-strong` at 2px."
    ]
  }
}